member.summary:
Snapshot of the file content the tab was opened with. Compared
against the live Monaco buffer to compute ;
rewritten on save so subsequent diff comparisons start fresh.

ILoggerProvider that pushes every log event into so the in-app Logs page can render them. Registered alongside the other logger providers (Console, Debug, …) via:
builder.Logging.AddProvider(new InMemoryLoggerProvider(store));
The provider doesn't filter — global filters are already applied by the .NET logging pipeline before log events reach us. If the Logs page wants a higher floor (e.g. drop Trace spam), filter at read time.

member.remarks:
The pipeline is built once and cached. Output is always a so callers can drop it directly into a Razor expression:
@MarkdownRenderer.Render(_body)
Content is trusted (bundled lesson files + user project files on the local machine). Markdig's default pipeline strips none of the tags, which is fine for our single-user desktop/web model; revisit if the curriculum ever starts loading Markdown from a remote source.

member.summary:
Splits a SourceKey of the form {abs-path}#package={X}
into its parts. Returns the raw path and a null package name when
no fragment is present (single-package files).
